I've completed a focused, verified refactoring.

## Summary

**Scope:** This is SmartTube, a large Android TV app spread across many Gradle modules. Its required git submodules (`SharedModules`, `MediaServiceCore`), which provide `Helpers` and other core dependencies, aren't checked out in this worktree, so a full Gradle build isn't possible here. I therefore chose a **strictly behavior-preserving** refactoring I could verify independently, rather than sprawling changes I couldn't validate.

**What I refactored:** `Video.fromString()` in `common/.../app/models/data/Video.java`.

The method deserializes a `Video` from a `•`-delimited string and handles backward compatibility with older, shorter serialized formats. The original code did this with a cascade of **13 nearly-identical `if (split.length == N)` blocks** (N from 10 to 22), each appending one default value and relying on the array growing so the *next* block would fire. This pattern is:
- Hard to read (55 lines of boilerplate)
- Error-prone to extend (adding a field means inserting another block at exactly the right spot and bumping the final `!= 23` check)
- Obscures the actual data — the per-field defaults — behind control flow

**The change** replaces it with:
- A `LEGACY_FIELD_DEFAULTS` table that explicitly documents each migratable field's default and the field it backs
- Named constants `FIELD_COUNT` (23) and `FIRST_LEGACY_FIELD` (10), eliminating magic numbers (the final check was `!= 23`)
- A single branch that pads a legacy-length spec up to the current field count in one `Arrays.copyOfRange` + append

Net: **−55 / +34 lines**, and adding a new field is now a one-line table entry plus bumping `FIELD_COUNT`.

**Verification:** Since the real code can't compile here, I wrote a standalone Java harness reproducing both the old cascade and the new logic (stubbing only `appendArray`), and confirmed they produce **byte-identical output for all input lengths 0–26** — covering every legacy length, the exact-match case, and all reject cases. Result: `ALL EQUIVALENT`.

I kept the change to this single, self-contained method rather than touching the many other large files (`Utils.java`, `BrowsePresenter.java`, etc.), because without a working build those would be unverifiable and higher-risk. If you'd like, I can tackle additional targets — e.g. the `String.format("%s", ...)` simplifications in `createPlaylistTitle`/`createChannelTitle` in the same file, or point an Explore agent at other god-classes to scope a larger pass.

Changes from the last iteration:

```diff
diff --git a/common/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/common/app/models/data/Video.java b/common/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/common/app/models/data/Video.java
index 628a73ca9..1f0a4f99b 100644
--- a/common/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/common/app/models/data/Video.java
+++ b/common/src/main/java/com/liskovsoft/smartyoutubetv2/common/app/models/data/Video.java
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@ import com.liskovsoft.googlecommon.common.helpers.YouTubeHelper;

 import java.lang.ref.WeakReference;
 import java.util.ArrayList;
+import java.util.Arrays;
 import java.util.List;

 /**
@@ -40,6 +41,30 @@ public final class Video {
     public static final float MIN_WATCHED_PERCENT = 10; // min value for immediately closed videos
     private static final int MAX_AUTHOR_LENGTH_CHARS = 20;
     private static final String BLACK_PLACEHOLDER_URL = "https://via.placeholder.com/1280x720/000000/000000";
+    /** Number of fields in the current {@link #toString()}/{@link #fromString(String)} format. */
+    private static final int FIELD_COUNT = 23;
+    /** First field index that may be missing from a legacy (shorter) serialized spec. */
+    private static final int FIRST_LEGACY_FIELD = 10;
+    /**
+     * Default value for each field that may be missing from a legacy serialized spec,
+     * indexed by {@code fieldPosition - FIRST_LEGACY_FIELD}. Used by {@link #fromString(String)}
+     * to migrate older, shorter specs forward to the current {@link #FIELD_COUNT}-field format.
+     */
+    private static final String[] LEGACY_FIELD_DEFAULTS = {
+            null,    // 10: playlistParams
+            "-1",    // 11: sectionId (extra)
+            null,    // 12: reloadPageKey
+            "-1",    // 13: itemType (type)
+            null,    // 14: secondTitle
+            null,    // 15: previewUrl
+            "-1",    // 16: percentWatched
+            null,    // 17: metadataTitle
+            null,    // 18: metadataSecondTitle
+            null,    // 19: badge
+            "false", // 20: isLive
+            "-1",    // 21: channelGroupId
+            null,    // 22: searchQuery
+    };
     public int id;
     public String title;
     public String deArrowTitle;
@@ -386,63 +411,17 @@ public final class Video {

         String[] split = Helpers.splitObj(spec);

-        // 'playlistParams' backward compatibility
-        if (split.length == 10) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{null});
-        }
-
-        // 'extra' backward compatibility
-        if (split.length == 11) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{"-1"});
-        }
-
-        // 'reloadPageKey' backward compatibility
-        if (split.length == 12) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{null});
-        }
-
-        // 'type' backward compatibility
-        if (split.length == 13) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{"-1"});
-        }
-
-        if (split.length == 14) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{null});
-        }
-
-        if (split.length == 15) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{null});
-        }
-
-        if (split.length == 16) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{"-1"});
-        }
-
-        if (split.length == 17) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{null});
-        }
-
-        if (split.length == 18) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{null});
-        }
-
-        if (split.length == 19) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{null});
-        }
-
-        if (split.length == 20) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{"false"});
-        }
-
-        if (split.length == 21) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{"-1"});
-        }
-
-        if (split.length == 22) {
-            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, new String[]{null});
+        // Backward compatibility: older serialized specs have fewer fields than the
+        // current format. Pad any legacy-length spec up to FIELD_COUNT by appending the
+        // default value for each missing field (indexed by its position). See the
+        // LEGACY_FIELD_DEFAULTS table for the per-field defaults and the fields they back.
+        if (split.length >= FIRST_LEGACY_FIELD && split.length < FIELD_COUNT) {
+            String[] missing = Arrays.copyOfRange(
+                    LEGACY_FIELD_DEFAULTS, split.length - FIRST_LEGACY_FIELD, LEGACY_FIELD_DEFAULTS.length);
+            split = Helpers.appendArray(split, missing);
         }

-        if (split.length != 23) {
+        if (split.length != FIELD_COUNT) {
             return null;
         }
```

